  "customfield_10231": {
    "value": "1. Given the component is rendered with a valid display prop, when it mounts, then the correct number of ProductCard instances are rendered matching the display value.\n2. Given showTitleAndLink=true and showLink=true, when the component renders, then the section header displays both the title and the link using the linkLabel value.\n3. Given showTitleAndLink=true and showLink=false, when the component renders, then the title is displayed but no link is shown.\n4. Given showTitleAndLink=false, when the component renders, then neither the title nor the link are displayed.\n5. Given the component is rendered with an empty or missing product array, when it mounts, then it renders no product cards and no error is thrown.\n6. Given the component is rendered at size=Desktop or size=Mobile, when it mounts, then the layout matches the corresponding Figma design spec variant.\n7. Given the section header is visible, when rendered, then the title is a semantically correct heading element and the link is a native anchor element with descriptive text.\n\nAccessibility\n8. Given the component is interactive, when a keyboard user navigates to the link, then it is reachable and activatable via keyboard alone.\n9. Given the component renders product cards, when a screen reader traverses the group, then each card is distinguishable and the group is appropriately labelled.\n10. Given the component is rendered, when tested against WCAG 2.1 AA criteria, then it passes with no violations.\n\n\n\n----\n\n*Tablet behaviour –* {{display=4}}\n\nThe {{size}} prop should also account for tablet. When the team configures {{display=4}}, tablet will only render 3 product cards — the 4th is hidden. This prevents an orphaned card from sitting awkwardly on its own row, as tablet uses a 3-column grid system."
