  "customfield_10231": {
    "value": "*Component configuration*\n\n# Given the component is rendered with showDescription=true, when the drawer opens, then a contextual description is displayed beneath the drawer header; when false, no description is rendered.\n# Given the component is rendered with showLanguageSelector=true, when the drawer opens, then a Language section with radio options is rendered below the country list; when false, no Language section is rendered.\n# Given the component is rendered with variant=\"country-currency-selector\", when the drawer opens, then the main content area renders the full country list grouped by region with currency codes alongside each country.\n\n*country-selector-dropdown atom (region groups)*\n\n# Given a region group is rendered, when in the collapsed state, then only the region label and chevron are visible and no country rows are shown beneath it.\n# Given a region group header is clicked or tapped, when toggled to expanded, then country rows appear beneath the header, each showing a flag icon, country name, and right-aligned currency code.\n# Given the drawer opens, when the shopper's current country falls within a region group, then that group renders in the expanded state with the current country's radio pre-selected.\n\n*Drawer shell and interaction*\n\n# Given the component is rendered, when it opens, then it slides in from the right on desktop and full-width on mobile leaving a small space open at the bottom, with a dark overlay backdrop.\n# Given the drawer is open, when the shopper scrolls the country list, then the drawer header and the Confirm footer remain sticky and the country list scrolls independently.\n# Given the shopper selects a country and presses the Apply CTA, when confirmed, then onConfirm(country, locale) fires with the selected values and the consuming page handles the redirect.\n# Given the drawer is open, when the shopper presses the close (x) icon or the backdrop, then the drawer closes without firing the callback and the prior selection is retained.\n\n*accessibility*\n\n# Given the component is rendered, when a keyboard user navigates, then focus is trapped within the open drawer, radio buttons are navigable via arrow keys, and closing the drawer returns focus to the trigger element.\n# Given the component renders on desktop, when viewed on mobile, then the drawer is full-width and all interactive elements meet minimum touch target size per the Design System spec.\n# Given the component is rendered, when a screen reader user interacts with the drawer, then the drawer is announced as a dialog with an accessible name, all interactive elements have descriptive labels, the accordion region groups expose expanded/collapsed state via aria-expanded, and the search field (if rendered) has an accessible label."
  },
